    "question_text": "Open fracture",
    "is_high_yield": true,
    "Core_Anatomy": "Bone metaphysis/diaphysis and surrounding soft tissue.",
    "Pathogenesis_Immediate": "An open fracture is a bone fracture communicating directly with an external wound in the overlying skin.",
    "Pathogenesis_Deep": "High-energy trauma forces sharp bone fragments through the skin, exposing the fracture hematoma and medullary cavity to environmental pathogens. This destroys the sterile environment necessary for healing and predeposits the site to chronic osteomyelitis.",
    "Why_Not": "A closed fracture maintains skin integrity, preserving the sterile fracture hematoma critical for early callus formation.",
    "Wow_Approach": "Open fractures are emergencies requiring aggressive sterile debridement, copious lavage (10+ liters), and rigid stabilization."
